---
import Exchange from "../layouts/Exchange.astro";
---
<Exchange title="Draft publisher terms" description="Development publisher terms. Public publishing remains disabled." active="publish">
<header class="workspace-heading terms-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Publisher agreement / Draft</p><h1>Publisher <em class="editorial-accent">terms.</em></h1><a href="/publish">Back to publishing ↗</a></header>
<article class="prose terms-copy">

      <p>
        Version 2026-09-24. These terms are a development placeholder and must be reviewed and
        replaced before public publishing is enabled.
      </p>
      <p>
        Publishers must have the rights to distribute every file in the package, must not include
        malware or undisclosed executable behavior, and must accurately describe permissions, data
        collection, support, and any external charges. Tabs may reject, quarantine, or revoke a
        version and retain review records. Approval is not a security certification.
      </p>
      <p>
        These draft terms do not replace a privacy policy, a complete legal agreement, or a security
        review. The Exchange operator must finalize all three before accepting public submissions.
      </p>
    </article></Exchange>
